<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">5 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 5 December, from 63 BCE to 1933.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">63 BCE <span class="tih-ago">1,963 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Senate condemns Catiline's fellow conspirators</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After Cicero's fourth speech against Catiline, and Cato's demand for severity, the Senate voted to execute five conspirators without trial. Cicero was hailed as saviour of the Republic but later exiled for it.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1360 CE <span class="tih-ago">666 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John II creates the first franc</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By an ordinance issued at Compiègne, the newly released John II of France created the gold franc, partly to raise his ransom. The franc remained the name of French currency until the euro.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1484 CE <span class="tih-ago">542 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Innocent VIII issues a bull against witchcraft</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The bull Summis desiderantes affectibus authorised the inquisitors Heinrich Kramer and Jacob Sprenger to pursue witches in Germany. Kramer printed it with his Malleus Maleficarum, fuelling later witch hunts.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/vienna" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vienna.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1791 CE <span class="tih-ago">235 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mozart dies in Vienna aged 35</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart died after a short illness, leaving his Requiem unfinished. In a career of barely three decades he wrote more than 600 works, including The Marriage of Figaro and The Magic Flute.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1933 CE <span class="tih-ago">93 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Prohibition ends in the United States</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Utah became the 36th state to ratify the 21st Amendment, repealing national Prohibition. The ban on alcohol had lasted almost 14 years and fed a boom in organised crime.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li></ol>
